      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town once hosted a station on the Minnesota and Manitoba Railroad, which later became part of the Canadian National Railway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baudette%2C_Minnesota",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Baudette sits where the Rainy River meets the Baudette River, forming a natural confluence right on the border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
